`never` is a type in TypeScript that represents a value that will never occur. It is used to indicate that a function or branch of code will never be reached, or that a value will never be of a certain type. For example, a function that always throws an error and never returns a value can be declared to have a return type of `never`. Using `never` can help catch errors and improve the type safety of your code.

