1. **Static Fields**: A static field is shared among all instances of a class. Each instance does not have its own copy of the static field. Instead, there is only one copy of the static field that is shared among all instances.

```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    public static int myStaticField;
}
```

2. **Static Properties**: A static property is a property that is associated with the type itself, rather than with an instance of the type. Like static fields, static properties are shared among all instances of a class.

```csharp
public class MyClass
{
    public static int MyStaticProperty
    {
        get;
        set;
    }
}
```

3. **Static Methods**: A static method can be called without creating an instance of the class. Static methods can only access other static members (fields, properties, methods) of the same class.

```csharp
