To create a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image, you can use the WordPress Block Editor (Gutenberg) and JavaScript. Here's a step-by-step guide to help you create a custom block:

1. Set up the development environment:
   - Install Node.js and npm (Node Package Manager)
   - Install the Gutenberg CLI: `npm install --global @wordpress/cli`
   - Install the Create Guten Block package: `npm install --save-dev @wordpress/create-block`

2. Create a new block directory:
   - Run the following command to create a new block: `wp create-block my-custom-block`
   - Navigate to the newly created directory: `cd my-custom-block`

3. Install dependencies:
   - Run `npm install` to install the necessary packages

4. Create the block:
   - In the `src/block` directory, create a new JavaScript file (e.g., `index.js`).
   - Import the necessary dependencies and define the block:

```javascript
import { registerBlockType } from '@wordpress/blocks';
import { RichText, MediaUpload, InspectorControls } from '@wordpress/editor';
import { Button } from '@wordpress/components';

registerBlockType('my-plugin/my-custom-block', {
    title: 'My Custom Block',
    icon: 'smiley',
    category: 'common',
    attributes: {
        title: {
            type: 'string',
            source: 'html',
            selector: 'h2',
        },
        content: {
            type: 'string',
            source: 'html',
            selector: 'p',
        },
        imageAlt: {
            attribute: 'alt',
            selector: '.my-image',
        },
        imageUrl: {
            attribute: 'src',
            selector: '.my-image',
        },
    },
    edit({ attributes, setAttributes }) {
        const { title, content, imageAlt, imageUrl } = attributes;

        return (
            <div className="my-custom-block">
                <InspectorControls key="inspector">
                    <MediaUpload
                        onSelect={(media) => {
                            setAttributes({ imageUrl: media.url, imageAlt: media.alt });
                        }}
                        type="image"
                        value={imageUrl}
                        render={({ open }) => (
                            <Button onClick={open}>Set image</Button>
                        )}
                    />
                </InspectorControls>
                <RichText
                    key="title"
                    tagName="h2"
                    placeholder="Title"
                    value={title}
                    onChange={(newTitle) => setAttributes({ title: newTitle })}
                />
                <RichText
                    key="content"
                    tagName="p"
                    placeholder="Content"
                    value={content}
                    onChange={(newContent) => setAttributes({ content: newContent })}
                />
                <img
                    src={imageUrl}
                    alt={imageAlt}
                    className="my-image"
                />
            </div>
        );
    },
    save({ attributes }) {
        const { title, content, imageAlt, imageUrl } = attributes;

        return (
            <div className="my-custom-block">
                <h2>{title}</h2>
                <p>{content}</p>
                <img src={imageUrl} alt={imageAlt} />
            </div>
        );
    },
});
```

5. Register the block in your plugin:
   - In the `src/index.js` file of your plugin, import and register the block:

```javascript
import { registerBlockType } from '@wordpress/blocks';
import MyCustomBlock from './my-custom-block/index';

registerBlockType('my-plugin/my-custom-block', MyCustomBlock);
```

